<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Poem of Almería</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1150</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Poema de Almería</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Poem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> is an incomplete <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> poem in hexameters, written in the mid-12th century and preserved with the Chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile">Alfonso the Emperor</a>. It celebrates the campaign of Alfonso VII of León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and his allies against Almería in 1147, describing the contingents of the army. It contains one of the earliest references to the Cid as 'Mio Cid'.</p></div>
